-- 09_synthesis_conflict_negative.cov
--
-- AUDIT FIXTURE, DOCUMENTATION-ONLY (not buildable via surface syntax).
--
-- Purpose : explain why the E601 detector exists and how it is exercised.
--
-- The Sprint 27 / PRELIM-005 audit finding (KSR-CVN-PRELIM-005) noted
-- that a user could shadow auto-synthesized ERC-20 functions (e.g.
-- `transfer`) with custom logic that violates the standard. The fix
-- was to add `strict_conflict_detection: true` (default in `StdlibConfig`)
-- so that the synthesizer aborts with E601 on conflict.
--
-- HOWEVER, in V0.9.0 surface syntax, `token` / `nft` / `registry` blocks
-- are metadata-only, they do NOT allow inline action / event / error
-- declarations. So the conflict path CANNOT be triggered from a .cov
-- source file alone in V0.9.0.
--
-- The E601 detector IS exercised via :
--   1. The build API (used by the playground), where pre-lowered IR
--      can include user-declared functions of the conflicting name.
--   2. The unit test :
--      `crates/covenant-stdlib/tests/unit.rs::user_transfer_strict_mode_emits_diag`
--   3. V0.9.x : when surface syntax extends token/nft/registry blocks
--      to allow custom actions, this fixture will become buildable
--      (and the conflict will fire at compile time).
--
-- Auditor checklist :
--   - The E601 long-form explanation MUST exist :
--       cargo run -- explain E601
--     Expected : "user-declared function conflicts with auto-synthesized
--     one ... strict mode catches the case where you accidentally
--     shadow the standard."
--   - The unit test MUST pass :
--       cargo test -p covenant-stdlib user_transfer_strict_mode
--   - Permissive mode MUST opt-in (StrictConflictDetection: false) :
--       cargo test -p covenant-stdlib user_transfer_permissive_mode
--
-- Documenting this surface-syntax gap explicitly so auditors don't
-- waste cycles trying to write a `.cov` file that triggers E601 from
-- source. The honest answer is : "you can't, in V0.9.0".

-- The pseudo-source below would produce E601 if surface syntax
-- supported it. PRESERVED AS DOCUMENTATION, NOT FOR COMPILATION.
--
-- token ConflictingCoin {
--     symbol: "CONFL"
--     name: "Conflicting Coin"
--     decimals: 18
--     supply: 1_000_000 to deployer
--     -- Hypothetical V0.9.x surface : custom action inside token block.
--     action transfer(to: address, value: amount) {
--         emit BadTransfer(caller, to, value)
--     }
--     event BadTransfer(from: address, to: address, value: amount)
-- }
--
-- Until V0.9.x extends the surface, this file is just a placeholder
-- record : it parses, emits a near-empty contract, and serves as the
-- carrier for the audit notes above.

record E601Placeholder {
    note: text = "see comments above"
}
